-- title:
--   A factorization of a prime times a unit has a unit factor
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a domain, $p\in A$ prime, $b$ a unit, and $x,y\in A$ with
--   $$
--   xy=p\,b .
--   $$
--
--   Then $x$ or $y$ is a unit. This is the base case of the local comparison induction: a norm of valuation one splits as a unit times a uniformizer.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/LinearAlgebra/CirculantHadamard/LocalComparisonInduction.lean#L19-L40

